Well, I got this problem: I was on my way back, talking to some other people
while I was playing and didn't notice that I was satiated and still trying to
eat something. Well I got that message "Stop eating?" but I was that busy with
talking (ja Michiel) and pressing the spacebar (--more--, you know) that I
didn't press the 'n' but instead the spacebar. Well I continued to eat and
my amulet of life saving disintegrated (or something like that) because of
choking over food (or something like that).

The problem is that when I accidentally hit my dog or some other peacefull
monster the question "Really attack? [yn]" will come up and hitting the
spacebar takes care of not attacking that monster. The default is 'n' which
is the best for you, but why is the default for "Stop eating? [yn]" also
'n' ?????

Shouldn't nethack take care of you and fill in what's best for you, in this
case 'y'? I did survive the game but I promised myself to never choke again
once I kept eating that black dragon...

Rather long story, isn't it? But I have something more...
Is it really true that throwing a potion of paralysis at the Wiz while standing
on a staircase up and after that climbing that stair makes the Wiz never come
back again??

I tried this at level 15 or so (when I was in Hell fighting the Wiz, I didn't
know (yet) the place of the staircase up and when I stould on that staircase
the Wiz wouldn't show) and indeed I never met the Wiz again. I did get that
message "You feel vaguely nervous" which makes me think the Wiz is coming.

I tried to read the sources but didn't find anything which could be a mistake
of me.

To those people who managed to take it to this point, please answer me!

